@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Medium composite-structure view — a PaymentGateway decomposed into 5 internal parts with boundary ports and delegation.
'   usecase:      Teach decomposition of one owner classifier into multiple parts, boundary ports, and delegation connectors to internal parts.
'   complexity:   medium
'   domain:       Payments
' ============================================================================
title Example Composite Structure - Medium Subsystem Decomposition

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' PaymentGateway is decomposed into five cooperating parts.  External actors
' only see the ports on the boundary; the internal wiring is an
' implementation detail.  Each port delegates to one internal part so the
' gateway can be treated as a black box by callers.
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rectangle "PaymentGateway" <<structuredClassifier>> as gw {

  ' ---- Boundary ports (provided/required interfaces) -------------------
  port "pReq : IChargeRequest"   as pReq   ' clients send charges here
  port "pRes  : IChargeResult"   as pRes   ' gateway emits results here
  port "pFraud : IFraudCheck"    as pFraud ' gateway calls external fraud svc
  port "pLedger : ILedger"       as pLedger' gateway calls external ledger

  ' ---- Internal parts (roles) ------------------------------------------
  component "api : ApiFacade"       as api
  component "fraud : FraudChecker"  as fraud
  component "auth : Authorizer"     as auth
  component "gateway : BankGateway" as bank
  component "audit : AuditLogger"   as audit

  ' ---- Internal connectors (collaboration wiring) ---------------------
  api --> fraud  : screen
  api --> auth   : authorize
  auth --> bank  : settle
  bank --> audit : record
  fraud --> audit : record

  ' ---- Delegation connectors (port <-> part) ---------------------------
  pReq    --> api
  api     --> pRes
  fraud   --> pFraud   ' required interface — gateway needs the external svc
  bank    --> pLedger  ' required interface — gateway needs the ledger
}

note right of gw
  <b>Black-box vs white-box</b>
  Externally only the four ports are
  visible (black box).  This diagram
  opens the box (white box) to show
  the five parts and how each port
  DELEGATES to an internal part.
  Provided ports (pReq, pRes) fulfil
  an interface the gateway offers.
  Required ports (pFraud, pLedger)
  name an interface the gateway NEEDS
  from its environment.
end note

@enduml
